Approach 3 — BFS + TreeMap

This is the standard and easiest approach for Bottom View.

And this is the code you provided.

The important advantage of BFS is that nodes are visited level by level.

Therefore, when we simply do:

map.put(hd, node.data);

a deeper node is naturally processed later and overwrites the previous node.

