The Most Important Difference: Top View vs Bottom View

This is extremely important for tree-view problems.

Top View

At each horizontal distance:

take FIRST node

Typical approach:

if (!map.containsKey(hd)) {
    map.put(hd, node.data);
}
Bottom View

At each horizontal distance:

take DEEPEST / LAST node

Typical BFS approach:

map.put(hd, node.data);

Because later BFS levels overwrite earlier ones.

